cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Waypoint in academic work, please cite this software. A DOI and the
  public repository URL will be added at release time; this file intentionally
  does not invent them.
title: >-
  Waypoint: a recovery-contract checker and mutation-calibration bed for agent
  and workflow runtimes
abstract: >-
  Waypoint provides a deterministic fault-injection calibration bed, a
  machine-checkable set of recovery contracts (C1-C6, S1-S3, plus
  log-integrity checks L1), a mutation-calibration gate (13 injected
  violations, zero false positives on a healthy baseline), and adapters that
  check real workflow frameworks against the same checker. This release is a
  research artifact: contracts an adapter cannot observe are labelled
  unobservable rather than silently passing.
authors:
  - family-names: Zhao
    given-names: Jie
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent runtime
  - workflow persistence
  - checkpoint and resume
  - recovery contract
  - mutation testing
  - reproducibility
